{{!-- Single document shell for every locale. {{{body}}} resolves inside a partial
     called from a layout (verified against Ghost 6.67), so default.hbs and the locale
     shells are one-liners that differ only in `lang`.
     `lang` is the BCP-47 tag for the collection's language; the default shell passes
     the site locale.

     Why the fallback is the site locale and not the post's language: a layout cannot
     see the post context. {{#has}} in a layout is always false, {{#post}} yields nothing
     there, and a {{#contentFor}} does reach the layout but is evaluated in the layout's
     own context, so a tag test inside it is false too (all three verified against Ghost
     6.67). The remedy is the documented one: a locale template on the post — which is
     what custom-es.hbs is. See docs/v3-roadmap.md, Phase 4 notes. --}}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{#if lang}}{{lang}}{{else}}{{@site.locale}}{{/if}}" class="dark">

<head>
    {{> "head"}}
</head>

<body class="{{body_class}} bg-dark-bg text-dark-text antialiased font-sans">

    {{> "header"}}

    <main id="main-wrapper" class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-6 relative mt-4">
        {{{body}}}
    </main>
    {{> "footer"}}

    {{ghost_foot}}

    {{> "scripts"}}
</body>

</html>
